  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/bms#HVACSystem">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/bms#BuildingSystem"/>
    <calculationFormula>Central chiller: A_eq=A_conditioned when observed; otherwise A_eq=GFA*p_conditioned when a building-specific or archetype-peer conditioned-area ratio is available; otherwise A_eq=GFA (full-conditioning fallback). Q_total=A_eq*q [cooling load, W]; N_chiller=Q_total/Q_each; S_chiller=N_chiller*w*p_i. Cooling tower: N_tower≈N_chiller; S=N_tower*w*p_i. Pump: N_pump≈2–3*N_chiller; S=N_pump*w*p_i. AHU: Q_air=k*Q_total/1000 [total supply airflow, m3/h, derived from the SAME Q_total as the chiller — NOT from a separate outdoor-air-only rate]; N_AHU=Q_air/q_AHU; S=N_AHU*w*p_i. Ductwork: Q_air=k*Q_total/1000; A_duct=(Q_air/N_f)/(3600*v); L_duct=GFA*gamma; S=2*(sqrt(A_duct)+sqrt(A_duct))*L_duct*T_duct*rho_i [square duct assumed]. Split: N_indoor=N_unit; S=N*w*p_i. Refrigerant pipe: L=k_layout*sqrt(GFA); S=L*w.</calculationFormula>
    <calculationFormula>IMPORTANT: airflowToCoolingLoadRatio (k, m3/h per kW) drives total AHU/ductwork supply airflow sizing and must NOT be confused with minOutdoorAirRate (SS553 Table 1, m3/h per m2), which is only the minimum fresh-air ventilation requirement by building type and is far smaller than total supply airflow (often 5-10x less, since most AHU supply air is recirculated, not fresh). Using the SS553 Table 1 fresh-air rate directly as the AHU sizing driver would undercount N_AHU and ductwork material stock.</calculationFormula>
    <applicabilityCondition>Central Chiller System applies when building function (bms:function) is A1 (Commercial), A2 (Office), C (Hotel/Hospital), or E (Educational/institutional) — building types regulated under SS553:2009, which scopes "commercial, office and institutional buildings" (excludes hospitals and residential; SS553 Clause 1.1, 1.4 also confirms no heating systems are needed in Singapore's climate) \citep{ss553-2009}. Split Unit System applies when building function is B1 (landed residential), B2 (condominium), or B3 (HDB) — multi-split systems are the standard residential ACMV practice in Singapore (HDB.gov.sg); centralised chiller cooling for residential remains a rare pilot exception (e.g., Tengah estate) as of 2026 and is not assumed by default. Condition parameter: hvacSystemType, derived from bms:function.</applicabilityCondition>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">DATA PROVENANCE NOTE: cooling load density (coolingLoadPerArea, q), cooling tower count ratio (N_tower≈N_chiller), pump count ratio (N_pump≈2-3*N_chiller), and the refrigerant pipe layout coefficient used in the Split Unit System branch are common preliminary engineering design heuristics rather than values codified in a single published standard (no authoritative source for these specific ratios was found despite literature search). They should be treated as adjustable defaults and calibrated against local design practice or manufacturer data where possible, not cited as standard-derived constants.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
